<title>UK: Unisource members to pool carrier operations-paper.</title>
<headline>Unisource members to pool carrier operations-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Members of European telecoms consortium Unisource are to merge their carrier services operations into a pan-European wholesaler, the Financial Times newspaper said.</p>
<p>Unisource's partners said such a merger would turn their carrier services into a $2.0 billion wholesaler.</p>
<p>The Unisource partners of Koninklijke PTT Nederland, Swiss Telecom PTT and Telia of Sweden are teamed up with U.S. group AT&amp;T Corp in a business communications venture called AT&amp;T Unisource.</p>
<p>Telefonica de Espana was asked to leave the Unisource group in late April after announcing it would join forces with Concert, a rival alliance between British Telecommunications and U.S.-based MCI Communications Corp.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
